Z||000002||Songman||05-29-2001||06:29 PM||||Loki...<P>I have it on the server as part of the Office 2000 Suite. You can get it if you want... but let me make a suggestion...<P>FrontPage has a compatibility problem between IE and Netscape. Your site will look fine in IE, but will be totally different in Netscape and any tricks you add in won't work...<P>The program you need to use to not have this problem is Adobe GoLive. I have versions 4 and 5 on the server. There is a bit of a learning curve but nothing that a couple of days can't fix. And of course, you can ask me any questions that you may have about the basics of it...<P>Here are a couple of my new sites made using GoLive 5. The first one is mine, the second one is my producer....<P> <A HREF="http://www.dalehouston.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.dalehouston.com</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.hankcochran.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.hankcochran.com</A> <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
